    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4f61295c-5449-5df4-9da5-c3caa918f54a",
      ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e87,-4,-3\u27e9$, $b=\u27e8-4,-6,7\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e8k,6,3\u27e9$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "20703eda-e951-5a94-a95f-c12f38f96758",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "1cfcd679-6c26-5382-be42-ae23698a35a4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{198}{23}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "1cfcd679-6c26-5382-be42-ae23698a35a4"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ k & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 7 \\\\ k & 3\\end{aligned}|)+((-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ k & 6\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot ((-6)\\cdot (3)-(7)\\cdot (6)))+((4)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (3)-(7)\\cdot (k)))+((-3)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (6)-(-6)\\cdot (k)))\\\\ &=((7)\\cdot (-60))+((4)\\cdot (-7k-12))+((-3)\\cdot (6k-24))\\\\ &=(-420)+(-28k-48)+(72-18k)\\\\ &=-46k-396\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-46k-396&=0\\\\ -46k&=396\\\\ k&=-\\frac{198}{23}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{198}{23}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
