      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & k & -5 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|)+((-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|)+((2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & k \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-7)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (2)-(-5)\\cdot (5)))+((-5)\\cdot ((-3)\\cdot (2)-(-5)\\cdot (2)))+((2)\\cdot ((-3)\\cdot (5)-(k)\\cdot (2)))\\\\ &=((-7)\\cdot (2k+25))+((-5)\\cdot (4))+((2)\\cdot (-2k-15))\\\\ &=(-14k-175)+(-20)+(-4k-30)\\\\ &=-18k-225\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18k-225&=0\\\\ -18k&=225\\\\ k&=-\\frac{25}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{25}{2}.$",
