  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186105908,
      "id": "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0",
      "title": "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "487c7642-993c-5cf8-8e3a-7cde0ec10ac0",
      ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e88,-7,-8\u27e9$, $b=\u27e84,-4,k\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e8-2,3,-3\u27e9$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "cea34117-38d8-5d2e-b775-108abc35ff41",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "5a01a313-6e2b-5465-9f23-a554cf602f2d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-2"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "5a01a313-6e2b-5465-9f23-a554cf602f2d"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}8 & -7 & -8 \\\\ 4 & -4 & k \\\\ -2 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|)+((7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|)+((-8)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (-3)-(k)\\cdot (3)))+((7)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (-3)-(k)\\cdot (-2)))+((-8)\\cdot ((4)\\cdot (3)-(-4)\\cdot (-2)))\\\\ &=((8)\\cdot (12-3k))+((7)\\cdot (2k-12))+((-8)\\cdot (4))\\\\ &=(96-24k)+(14k-84)+(-32)\\\\ &=-10k-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10k-20&=0\\\\ -10k&=20\\\\ k&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
